! Setup

There is nothing to configure to get started.

# Post a link to your tiddler on Mastodon.
# Copy the link of that post.
# Add a `mastodon-post` field to the tiddler and paste the link as its value.

A ''Show Mastodon comments'' button then appears at the bottom of the tiddler, and a Mastodon button in its toolbar. Tiddlers without the field are left alone.

The field accepts:

* `https://mastodon.social/@user/117382963679112384`
* `https://instance.example/@user@other.domain/117382963679112384`
* `https://instance.example/users/user/statuses/117382963679112384`

Only `http` and `https` links are accepted.

!! What is shown

* The author of each reply, with avatar, name and account
* Content warnings, collapsed by default
* Sanitized status content, with links and custom emojis
* The date, linking to the reply on Mastodon
* Image attachments and preview cards
* Replies, boosts and favourites counts, unless turned off in the [[settings|$:/plugins/breakzplatform/mastodon-comments/settings/settings]]
* Nested replies, up to the configured depth. Deeper conversations get a link to continue on Mastodon

!! What is hidden

* Replies whose visibility is not public or unlisted
* Sensitive image attachments until the reader opens them
* Deleted replies, replies not returned by the instance, and replies beyond the configured depth

When replies are hidden or beyond the depth limit, a short link points to the full thread on Mastodon.

